<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <!--
      SPRING BOOT VERSION DECISION : CONFIRMED, DELIBERATE (NOT AN UNRESOLVED RISK).
      The parent below pins spring-boot-starter-parent 3.5.16: the highest patch of the
      Spring Boot 3.x line, exactly as mandated by AAP sections 0.5.1 and 0.7.2, which
      "explicitly pin 'Spring Boot 3.x'", so the target pins the highest 3.x patch
      (3.5.16).

      DECISION (confirmed in refinement): this release REMAINS on Spring Boot 3.5.16 by
      design. This is a settled, intentional engineering decision — NOT an open question
      and NOT an unresolved risk. The module is deliberately NOT upgraded to the 4.1.x
      line, and NO dependency version in this pom.xml is changed as part of this decision.
      What was previously tracked as the "3.5.16 EOL" risk (originally surfaced as QA
      F-14, INFO / dependency-lifecycle) is hereby CLOSED as an accepted, dispositioned
      decision.

      Known lifecycle fact (context only): the Spring Boot 3.5 line reached OPEN-SOURCE
      end-of-life on 2026-06-30, so 3.5.16 no longer receives free community patches. AAP
      section 0.7.2 records the migration to the (also Java-17-compatible) Spring Boot
      4.1.x line as an "optional forward path (advisory, not adopted)"; the AAP is the
      frozen, agreed-upon source of truth, so changing the major line is out of scope for
      this module and would require an explicit AAP revision and approval, not a unilateral
      bump here.

      PLANNED FUTURE UPGRADE WINDOW (deployment governance): securing a supported channel
      is scheduled as a separate, tested change — either (a) commercial / extended support
      for the 3.x line (VMware Tanzu Spring), or (b) an approved, scheduled migration to
      the 4.1.x line. This is documented in README.md under "Dependency and framework
      lifecycle".

      NOTE: this is a framework-version/support decision ONLY. No confirmed application-
      library CVE is attributed to Spring Boot 3.5.16; the security overrides declared in
      the properties and dependencyManagement blocks below independently pin remediated
      versions of the transitive libraries that DID have published advisories.
    -->
    <parent>
        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>
        <version>3.5.16</version>
        <relativePath/>
    </parent>

    <groupId>com.aws.carddemo</groupId>
    <artifactId>account-service</artifactId>
    <version>0.0.1-SNAPSHOT</version>
    <packaging>jar</packaging>

    <name>account-service</name>
    <description>CardDemo Account Management microservice (Feature F-003) - account inquiry and update</description>

    <properties>
        <java.version>17</java.version>
        <springdoc.version>2.8.17</springdoc.version>

        <!--
          Security dependency overrides (centrally managed).
          These properties override the versions the spring-boot-starter-parent:3.5.16
          BOM would otherwise resolve, pinning each affected library to a fixed-or-newer
          release that remediates known published vulnerabilities. They are parent-
          compatible patch/minor bumps within the same line, so they do not change any
          API used by the module. Reviewed and bumped as a set; revisit on each Boot/BOM
          upgrade so the overrides never silently mask a newer managed fix.
            * tomcat.version        10.1.55 -> 10.1.57  (embedded Tomcat, via spring-boot-starter-web)
            * jackson-bom.version   2.21.4  -> 2.21.5   (whole Jackson BOM incl. jackson-databind)
            * postgresql.version    42.7.11 -> 42.7.12  (pgJDBC driver)
            * commons-lang3.version 3.17.0  -> 3.18.0   (transitive via spring-core/tomcat)
            * logback.version       1.5.36  -> 1.5.38   (logback-core + logback-classic; CVE-2026-13006)
          The test-scope commons-compress override is applied via <dependencyManagement>
          below because it is NOT a spring-boot-starter-parent managed property.
        -->
        <tomcat.version>10.1.57</tomcat.version>
        <jackson-bom.version>2.21.5</jackson-bom.version>
        <postgresql.version>42.7.12</postgresql.version>
        <commons-lang3.version>3.18.0</commons-lang3.version>
        <logback.version>1.5.38</logback.version>
    </properties>

    <!--
      Centrally managed version overrides for transitive dependencies that are NOT
      exposed as spring-boot-starter-parent properties. Declaring them here forces the
      chosen version everywhere they appear in the graph, regardless of scope.

      commons-compress: Testcontainers (test scope) pulls in commons-compress 1.24.0,
      which is affected by CVE-2024-25710 and CVE-2024-26308 (archive-processing
      denial-of-service). Apache fixes these in 1.26.0; we pin 1.27.1 (the current
      stable line, >= the 1.26.0 fix) which remains API-compatible with Testcontainers
      1.21.4's archive handling.

      swagger-ui: springdoc-openapi-starter-webmvc-ui 2.8.17 transitively bundles the
      org.webjars:swagger-ui 5.32.2 front-end, which embeds DOMPurify 3.3.2. That
      DOMPurify build is inside the vulnerable range 3.0.1-3.3.3 (CVE-2026-41238 /
      CVE-2026-41239 / CVE-2026-41240 - prototype-pollution / template-sanitizer
      bypass XSS; CWE-79 / CWE-1321) and is served on the unauthenticated Swagger UI
      surface. We pin swagger-ui 5.32.8 (the first 5.32.x patch that bundles DOMPurify
      >= 3.4.0 - specifically 3.4.11 - remediating all three CVEs). 5.32.8 is the same
      minor line as 2.8.17's default 5.32.2, so it is a drop-in, API-compatible patch
      that keeps springdoc pinned at the AAP-mandated 2.8.17 (§0.5.1: the 2.x line for
      Spring Boot 3.x) while removing the vulnerable component from the runtime jar.
    -->
    <dependencyManagement>
        <dependencies>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>org.apache.commons</groupId>
                <artifactId>commons-compress</artifactId>
                <version>1.27.1</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>org.webjars</groupId>
                <artifactId>swagger-ui</artifactId>
                <version>5.32.8</version>
            </dependency>
        </dependencies>
    </dependencyManagement>

    <dependencies>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-data-jpa</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-validation</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-actuator</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.postgresql</groupId>
            <artifactId>postgresql</artifactId>
            <scope>runtime</scope>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.flywaydb</groupId>
            <artifactId>flyway-core</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.flywaydb</groupId>
            <artifactId>flyway-database-postgresql</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springdoc</groupId>
            <artifactId>springdoc-openapi-starter-webmvc-ui</artifactId>
            <version>${springdoc.version}</version>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-test</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.testcontainers</groupId>
            <artifactId>postgresql</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.testcontainers</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
                <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>

            <!--
              Surefire runs the FAST tests during `mvn test`: plain unit tests and
              @WebMvcTest slices. It EXCLUDES *IntegrationTest AND *PerformanceTest so the
              Testcontainers-backed @SpringBootTest tests (which require a Docker daemon) do
              NOT run in the ordinary `test` phase. Surefire's default include (**/*Test.java)
              would otherwise pick up AccountApiIntegrationTest and AccountPerformanceTest and
              force every `mvn test` (and every `mvn package`) to require Docker. Both slow,
              Docker-backed suites therefore run only in the `verify` phase via Failsafe below.
              Version is managed by spring-boot-starter-parent.
            -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
                <configuration>
                    <excludes>
                        <exclude>**/*IntegrationTest.java</exclude>
                        <exclude>**/*PerformanceTest.java</exclude>
                    </excludes>
                </configuration>
            </plugin>

            <!--
              Failsafe runs the SLOW, Docker-backed tests during `mvn verify` (integration-test
              then verify goals). It INCLUDES *IntegrationTest (the AAP-named convention,
              AAP section 0.3.1) AND *PerformanceTest, neither of which Failsafe's default
              *IT / IT* / *ITCase patterns match, so `mvn verify` executes the Surefire suite
              PLUS AccountApiIntegrationTest and AccountPerformanceTest against a real
              PostgreSQL provisioned by Testcontainers. AccountPerformanceTest validates the
              <=2s response-time target (Technical Specification section 2.4.2.1) under
              concurrent load; like the integration test it needs a Docker daemon, so it is
              deliberately kept out of the Docker-free `test` phase. The bound `verify` goal
              fails the build if any integration OR performance test failed. Version is
              managed by spring-boot-starter-parent.
            -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-failsafe-plugin</artifactId>
                <configuration>
                    <includes>
                        <include>**/*IntegrationTest.java</include>
                        <include>**/*PerformanceTest.java</include>
                    </includes>
                </configuration>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <id>integration-tests</id>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>integration-test</goal>
                            <goal>verify</goal>
                        </goals>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>

</project>
